ARC-AGI-3 accelerator pool from H100 to `g4-standard-48` on 2026-05-07
(Kaggle staff announcement) -- Google Cloud's own machine-type docs
identify that as one NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition GPU
with 96GB GDDR7, not the 16GB T4 / 24GB L4 our own submission-
requirements doc (dated 2026-06-17, six weeks AFTER the swap) still
assumes. forge's own winning, scored Kaggle notebook (3rd place, LB
0.86) explicitly ran Gemma-4-31B-it on "RTX Pro 6000" -- direct
confirmation the 96GB hardware is real and scores successfully in this
competition.

Operator decision: queue as a task (13, high priority) rather than
investigate further or touch the frozen config this session. Includes an
honest caveat (could not find explicit Kaggle confirmation the hidden
scored backend is bit-identical to the visible notebook env) and a
four-step plan for whoever picks it up: re-confirm the scored backend,
offline A/B a larger generator, check MTP compatibility at the larger
size, and require an explicit operator decision before touching the
frozen live-submission config -- same discipline as task 7.

